      },
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "PATHO: appears to be mediated by activation of CD4+ & CD8+ T lymphocytes; most often occurs 2-6wks after medication initiation"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
       "indLeft": 0,
       "indRight": 0,
       "indFirst": 0,
       "spaceBefore": 0,
       "spaceAfter": 0,
       "line": null,
       "align": "left",
       "shade": null,
       "borders": null,
       "marker": null
      },
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Etiology: MCC are anticonvulsants (phenobarbital, carbamazepine phenytoin, lamotrigine), minocycline, sulfa abx"
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "slide_card",
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
       "indLeft": 0,
       "indRight": 0,
       "indFirst": 0,
       "spaceBefore": 0,
       "spaceAfter": 0,
       "line": null,
       "align": "left",
       "shade": null,
       "borders": null,
       "marker": null
      },
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Presentation"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
       "indLeft": 0,
       "indRight": 0,
       "indFirst": 0,
       "spaceBefore": 0,
       "spaceAfter": 0,
       "line": null,
       "align": "left",
       "shade": null,
       "borders": null,
       "marker": null
      },
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Prodrome: fever, pharyngitis, malaise 2-3d before rash onset"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
       "indLeft": 0,
       "indRight": 0,
       "indFirst": 0,
       "spaceBefore": 0,
       "spaceAfter": 0,
       "line": null,
       "align": "left",
       "shade": null,
       "borders": null,
       "marker": null
      },
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Skin: morbilliform exanthem w/ accentuation on face, upper trunk, proximal extremities; may progress to erythroderma; pruritis common"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
       "indLeft": 0,
       "indRight": 0,
       "indFirst": 0,
       "spaceBefore": 0,
       "spaceAfter": 0,
       "line": null,
       "align": "left",
       "shade": null,
       "borders": null,
       "marker": null
      },
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "desquamation develops days-weeks after initial eruption; can last several weeks"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
       "indLeft": 0,
       "indRight": 0,
       "indFirst": 0,
       "spaceBefore": 0,
       "spaceAfter": 0,
       "line": null,
       "align": "left",
       "shade": null,
       "borders": null,
       "marker": null
      },
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Other manifestations: facial edema (esp. periorbital), LAD, mucosal involvement (cheilitis, pharyngeal erythema)"
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "slide_card",
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
